  "id": "subtraction-method",
  "term": "subtraction method",
  "definition": "The subtraction method is a restricted-diffusion imaging approach that compares two apparent diffusion coefficient maps made from diffusion-weighted images collected with short versus long effective diffusion times. It produces an image from the difference between those ADC maps to highlight diffusion-related changes.",
